<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Boju</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">506 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Boju was fought in 506 BCE in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubei">Hubei</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-helu-of-wu">King Helü of Wu</a>, advised by the Chu exile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zixu">Wu Zixu</a> and traditionally by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-tzu">Sun Wu</a>, invaded Chu and defeated its main army. Wu forces then took the Chu capital Ying, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-zhao-of-chu">King Zhao of Chu</a> fled. Chu survived only after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> sent an army in response to the pleas of the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shen-baoxu">Shen Baoxu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-boju.jpg" alt="Battle of Boju" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Boju.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
